{"name":"Blue Sash","hex":"#494d58","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"sash","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of cloth designed to be worn around the waist.","A decorative length of cloth worn over the shoulder to the opposite hip, often for ceremonial or other formal occasions."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn with a sash."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sciarpa azzurra","blocks":[{"text":"The sciarpa azzurra is a typical external ornament used as part of the uniforms of the Officers of the Italian Armed Forces and the Italian Police Corps, worn around the neck or tied around the waist in particular circumstances."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Cerimonia_Scuola_applicazione.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sciarpa_azzurra"},{"title":"Sash","blocks":[{"text":"A sash is a large and usually colorful ribbon or band of material worn around the human body, either draping from one shoulder to the opposing hip and back up, or else encircling the waist. The sash around the waist may be worn in daily attire, but the sash from shoulder to hip is typically only worn on ceremonial occasions. Ceremonial sashes are also found in a V-shaped format, draping straight from both shoulders down, intersecting and forming an angle over the chest or abdomen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Philip_V_of_Spain.jpg/330px-Philip_V_of_Spain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sash"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/2june_2007_417.jpg/120px-2june_2007_417.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/2june_2007_417.jpg/250px-2june_2007_417.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/2june_2007_417.jpg/120px-2june_2007_417.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2june_2007_417.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/2june_2007_392.jpg/120px-2june_2007_392.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/2june_2007_392.jpg/250px-2june_2007_392.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org